# Laravel API Best Practices

## Request Flow
Route → FormRequest validation → Controller → Service → Model → Response

## Controllers (Thin)
public function store(StoreRequest $request): JsonResponse
{
    $item = $this->service->create($request->validated());
    return response()->json($item, 201);
}

## Services (Business Logic)
public function create(array $data): Model
{
    return DB::transaction(fn() => Model::create($data));
}

## Models
protected $fillable = ['name', 'email'];
protected $casts = ['is_active' => 'boolean', 'data' => 'array'];
public function items(): HasMany { return $this->hasMany(Item::class); }

## Validation (FormRequest)
public function rules(): array {
    return ['email' => 'required|email|unique:users'];
}

## Queries
Model::with('relation')->where('status', 'active')->paginate(20);

## Responses
Success: response()->json($data, 200)
Created: response()->json($data, 201)
Error: response()->json(['error' => 'message'], 400)

## Must Use
- Eager loading: ->with()
- Transactions: DB::transaction()
- Type hints everywhere
- API Resources for output
- Rate limiting

## Avoid
N+1 queries | Fat controllers | $guarded=[] | Raw SQL | Logic in migrations